Title: Into the Pyramid
Order: 14
Production Code: 1x14

EXT. EXPEDITION CAMP - DAY

AMB: subdued camp noise

The mail brings the news [[Reuel Briggs]] has been dreading: [[Dianthe Lusk]], drowned, weeks ago, on the Charles River. He collapses. For three weeks [[Professor Stone]] and [[Charlie Vance]] nurse him through a breakdown too total for words.

REUEL BRIGGS
(hollow, to no one)
Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it.

EXT. MEROE - NIGHT (LATER)

SFX: oars in still water

Leaving only a note for Charlie that he has gone to the third pyramid and not to worry, Reuel rows himself across to Meroe by moonlight, revolver in hand, no plan beyond losing himself in the pyramid the way he's lost everything else.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID - NIGHT

SFX: footsteps echoing in a vast empty chamber

He descends past glass cases of the ancient dead, down steps cut in granite to a ledge around what was once a tank, searching for the Sphinx's head the parchment described — and finds it, the devilish countenance of the Ethiopian Sphinx in his candle's light.

A hand seems to pass before his face out of the darkness, trailing a strange sweetness.

REUEL BRIGGS
(faint)
What—

He falls.

INT. TELASSAR - RECEIVING CHAMBER - DAY (FOUR DAYS LATER)

AMB: fountains, distant music, an unfamiliar hush

Reuel wakes on silk cushions in a marble hall that has no business existing. [[Ai]] stands over him.

REUEL BRIGGS
(impetuously)
Where am I? How came I here?

AI
(in ancient Arabic)
Peace. You have nothing to fear. You are in the hidden city Telassar. In my people you will behold the direct descendants of the inhabitants of Meroe. I am Ai, the faithful prime minister of our king who is to come.
